From: mitzev <ogi@kunasystems.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Apr 2026 02:06:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?P09.48:=20#[rustc=5Fswift=5Fthrows]=20+=20Swift?=
 =?UTF-8?q?Error=20=E2=80=94=20Swift=20throwing=20fns=20(1.02=20throws)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ships Swift `throws` interop: `extern "Swift"` foreign-fn decls
marked `#[rustc_swift_throws]` attach LLVM's `swifterror`
attribute to their last parameter, pinning it to the Swift-ABI
error register (r12 on x86_64, x21 on aarch64 Darwin) per the
Swift calling convention. Both function declarations and call
sites get the attribute, so throwing calls round-trip through
LLVM's register-allocation machinery without any hand-rolled
register-move plumbing.

Closes the most-commonly-cited Swift interop gap I called out in
the 1.02 scope discussion.

Plumbing:

- compiler/rustc_llvm/llvm-wrapper/RustWrapper.cpp: new
  `LLVMRustAttributeKind::SwiftError = 50` variant + mapping to
  LLVM's `Attribute::SwiftError` in `fromRust`.
- compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/llvm/ffi.rs: mirror Rust-side
  `AttributeKind::SwiftError` enumerator.
- compiler/rustc_span/src/symbol.rs: +`rustc_swift_throws`.
- compiler/rustc_feature/src/builtin_attrs.rs: register the attr.
- compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs: new
  `AttributeKind::RustcSwiftThrows(Span)` variant.
- compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/encode_cross_crate.rs: Yes (attr
  travels across crates).
- compiler/rustc_passes/src/check_attr.rs: include in the
  accepted-without-target-check list.
- compiler/rustc_attr_parsing/src/attributes/codegen_attrs.rs:
  `RustcSwiftThrowsParser` via the P09.43 `rustcc_noargs_attr!`
  macro, allowed on `Target::ForeignFn`.
- compiler/rustc_attr_parsing/src/context.rs: register the parser.
- compiler/rustc_middle/src/middle/codegen_fn_attrs.rs: new
  `CodegenFnAttrFlags::SWIFT_ERROR_LAST_ARG = 1 << 19`.
- compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/codegen_attrs.rs: set the flag
  on the callee's CodegenFnAttrs when the attr is present.
- compiler/rustc_target/src/callconv/mod.rs: new
  `FnAbi::swift_error_last_arg: bool`. Static-size assert bumped
  80 → 88.
- compiler/rustc_ty_utils/src/abi.rs: populate the new FnAbi
  field from `codegen_fn_attrs`.
- compiler/rustc_codegen_gcc/src/int.rs: default the field to
  false in its synthetic FnAbi.
- compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/abi.rs: `apply_attrs_llfn` +
  `apply_attrs_callsite` attach SwiftError to the last LLVM
  argument (`Argument(i - 1)` after the normal arg loop) when
  `swift_error_last_arg` is set.

User-facing shape:

```rust
use rustcc_swift_rt::SwiftError;

unsafe extern "Swift" {
    #[rustc_swift_throws]
    #[link_name = "$s5MyLib8do_thingSiSiAA5InputVtKF"]
    fn do_thing_raw(
        input: i64,
        err: *mut *mut core::ffi::c_void,
    ) -> i64;
}

fn do_thing(input: i64) -> Result<i64, SwiftError> {
    let mut err: *mut core::ffi::c_void = core::ptr::null_mut();
    let ret = unsafe { do_thing_raw(input, &mut err) };
    if err.is_null() {
        Ok(ret)
    } else {
        Err(unsafe { SwiftError::from_retained(err) })
    }
}
```

Validation:

- `cargo check compiler` → clean.
- `./x.py build --stage 1 library` → clean.
- /tmp/p09-48-swift-throws/ probe: emitted LLVM IR contains
  `declare swiftcc i64 @"..."(i64, ptr swifterror)` on the
  declaration and `call swiftcc i64 @"..."(i64 %input, ptr
  swifterror %err)` on the call site. That's what the Swift
  ABI wants LLVM to see.
- rustcc workspace: cargo test --workspace → 235/0 (unchanged).

Not done / scope notes:

- SwiftError wrapper + #[rustc_swift_throws] declaration work;
  end-to-end runtime round-trip requires linking against a real
  Swift runtime (which ships its own `swift_retain`/`swift_release`
  and actually respects the swifterror register convention at
  call time). In-tree probe exercises only the Rust-side ownership
  semantics (from_retained / into_raw / is_null / Drop); runtime
  integration against a Swift library is a user-side concern.
- Last-argument convention is positional for now. Future work
  could add a per-arg `#[rustc_swift_error_slot]` attribute for
  non-last placements, matching Swift's own flexibility — but
  every Swift throwing fn the ABI emits has the error slot as
  the implicit trailing hidden arg anyway, so last-arg covers
  100% of expected use.

